---
layout: null
sitemap: false
---
{%- comment -%}
Overrides jekyll-sitemap, which takes lastmod from page.last_modified_at or
page.date — and a collection document with neither falls back to the build
time, so every deploy claimed all 28 pages had just changed. A sitemap with no
lastmod tells crawlers nothing, which is better than telling them something
untrue. Restore the field the day pages carry a real modification date.
{%- endcomment -%}
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
{%- assign pages = site.pages | where_exp: "p", "p.sitemap != false" -%}
{%- for page in pages -%}
{%- if page.url contains '.html' or page.url contains '.xml' or page.url contains '.txt' -%}
{%- unless page.url == '/index.html' -%}{% continue %}{%- endunless -%}
{%- endif %}
  <url><loc>{{ page.url | replace: '/index.html', '/' | absolute_url | xml_escape }}</loc></url>
{%- endfor -%}
{%- for doc in site.docs %}
  <url><loc>{{ doc.url | absolute_url | xml_escape }}</loc></url>
{%- endfor %}
</urlset>
